meta {
  name: Budget projection
  type: http
  seq: 1
}

get {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/projections/budget?granularity=month&currency=CAD&asOf={{today}}
  body: none
  auth: inherit
}

params:query {
  granularity: month
  currency: CAD
  asOf: {{today}}
  ~from: {{today}}
  ~to: 2027-02-28
  ~accountId: acc_chequing
  ~includeScheduled: true
  ~includeCategoryBudgets: true
}

assert {
  res.status: eq 200
}

docs {
  User story 4. Where the total balance is heading.
  
  **The rule that makes it coherent:** dates up to and including `asOf` use
  **actual transactions**; dates after it use **scheduled occurrences that have
  not been posted**. Without that split, a rent payment that already cleared
  would be counted once as a transaction and again as this month's bill.
  
  The consequence is that the bucket containing `asOf` is a hybrid — part
  history, part forecast. It is flagged `isPartiallyProjected`, and `actual` and
  `scheduled` stay separate in every bucket so the client can render the seam
  however it likes. `closingBalance` chains:
  `closing[n] === closing[n-1] + net[n]`.
  
  Deliberately excluded: paused items, occurrences already posted or skipped,
  transfers, and **discretionary spending** — this is a commitments forecast, not
  a behavioural model. `includeCategoryBudgets=true` bolts on a crude estimate
  from the monthly category budgets and labels it an assumption, not a fact.
  
  `asOf` is movable, so you can ask what last month's projection would have said.
}
